Fix sign extension of libmongoc's SSL_CTX options

_mongoc_openssl_ctx_new() keeps the SSL_CTX options in an int. SSL_OP_ALL
includes SSL_OP_CRYPTOPRO_TLSEXT_BUG (bit 31), so the value is negative and
SSL_CTX_set_options(), which takes a uint64_t since OpenSSL 3.0, receives it
sign-extended with bits 32-63 set, turning on options nobody asked for.
OpenSSL 4.0 assigns SSL_OP_ECH_GREASE to bit 37, so every TLS connection
offers an ECH GREASE extension. Generating it needs an X25519 key, which
fails when X25519 is not available (e.g. with the FIPS provider), and the
handshake aborts before the ClientHello is sent:

  TLS handshake failed: error:0308010C:digital envelope routines::unsupported

Store the options in a uint64_t.

libmongoc 2.5.9, which this driver bundles, still has the int upstream. PHP
had the same defect in its own TLS streams; os/php-8.6 carries
openssl-ssl-ctx-options-uint64.patch for it.

diff --git a/src/libmongoc/src/libmongoc/src/mongoc/mongoc-openssl.c b/src/libmongoc/src/libmongoc/src/mongoc/mongoc-openssl.c
index ea09a7c..4699dfa 100644
--- a/src/libmongoc/src/libmongoc/src/mongoc/mongoc-openssl.c
+++ b/src/libmongoc/src/libmongoc/src/mongoc/mongoc-openssl.c
@@ -931,7 +931,7 @@ SSL_CTX *
 _mongoc_openssl_ctx_new(mongoc_ssl_opt_t *opt)
 {
    SSL_CTX *ctx = NULL;
-   int ssl_ctx_options = 0;
+   uint64_t ssl_ctx_options = 0;
 
    /*
     * Ensure we are initialized. This is safe to call multiple times.
